{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"76.68.33.151","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b7c8a1d710d04e93a73ffae4b31aff65","RawContent":"&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;Well, I guess it is my turn to start my own planning thread! &amp;nbsp;I had read so many helpful planning threads on this awesome forum and I thought I would do the same.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;I am 124 days away until my wedding (but who is counting) and I thought I would post my ideas to not only help others, but also as a way to keep me accountable to my planning. &amp;nbsp; I have truly loved reading other bride&#039;s planning threads and will try to share as much as possible to help someone else in their early stages of planning. &amp;nbsp;The benefits of the forum have been so great and I am so grateful for the generous brides that have been so busy planning their own fabulous weddings and still made it a priority to share for the rest of us. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;We are getting married June 20, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess. &amp;nbsp;We have been to this resort twice and love, love, love, love it!! &amp;nbsp;We are really looking forward to going back and just feeling absolutely confident in the service and quality of the hotel. &amp;nbsp;So my head has been clouded with to-do lists and I had been really overwhelmed as soon as we transitioned from 2014 to 2015. &amp;nbsp;I have a destination wedding planner but I found that it was easy to tuck it away and it is over 200 pages so it&#039;s easy to miss a section. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;We decided to experiment with a wall map. &amp;nbsp;We put up some bristol board on a wall at home and my fiance and I started posting all the random things that we need to get done. &amp;nbsp;All those little things like, \"ask our flower girl\" &amp;nbsp;or \"write vows\" or \"lose 60lbs\" haha.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;After mapping out our to do list it really helped put everything into perspective. &amp;nbsp;As we get things done, we remove the sticky, and as we think of more things to do, we slap them on. &amp;nbsp;It has really helped out and I have a better sense of what still needs to get done! &amp;nbsp;Yay planning! &amp;nbsp;xo&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[{"Id":30639,"Name":"IMG_2451.JPG","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_02_2015\/post-277519-0-72775200-1424146653.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_02_2015\/post-277519-0-72775200-1424146653_thumb.jpg","Width":1000,"Height":1000}],"Id":1886526,"PostDate":1424128728,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">Well, I guess it is my turn to start my own planning thread! \u00a0I had read so many helpful planning threads on this awesome forum and I thought I would do the same.<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">I am 124 days away until my wedding (but who is counting) and I thought I would post my ideas to not only help others, but also as a way to keep me accountable to my planning. \u00a0 I have truly loved reading other bride's planning threads and will try to share as much as possible to help someone else in their early stages of planning. \u00a0The benefits of the forum have been so great and I am so grateful for the generous brides that have been so busy planning their own fabulous weddings and still made it a priority to share for the rest of us. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">We are getting married June 20, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess. \u00a0We have been to this resort twice and love, love, love, love it!! \u00a0We are really looking forward to going back and just feeling absolutely confident in the service and quality of the hotel. \u00a0So my head has been clouded with to-do lists and I had been really overwhelmed as soon as we transitioned from 2014 to 2015. \u00a0I have a destination wedding planner but I found that it was easy to tuck it away and it is over 200 pages so it's easy to miss a section. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">We decided to experiment with a wall map. \u00a0We put up some bristol board on a wall at home and my fiance and I started posting all the random things that we need to get done. \u00a0All those little things like, \"ask our flower girl\" \u00a0or \"write vows\" or \"lose 60lbs\" haha.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">After mapping out our to do list it really helped put everything into perspective. \u00a0As we get things done, we remove the sticky, and as we think of more things to do, we slap them on. \u00a0It has really helped out and I have a better sense of what still needs to get done! \u00a0Yay planning! \u00a0xo<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10747;0\/st\/20150620\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/f3ff\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1396964852,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1428501609","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":196,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"db6b0d2aeeaa0b6ba30863fd9bfc0397","RawContent":"[quote name=\"veryvalero\" post=\"1886526\" timestamp=\"1424146728\"]\n[color=rgb(40,40,40)][font=arial]\nWell, I guess it is my turn to start my own planning thread!  I had read so many helpful planning threads on this awesome forum and I thought I would do the same.[\/font][\/color][color=rgb(40,40,40)][font=arial]\nI am 124 days away until my wedding (but who is counting) and I thought I would post my ideas to not only help others, but also as a way to keep me accountable to my planning.   I have truly loved reading other bride&#039;s planning threads and will try to share as much as possible to help someone else in their early stages of planning.  The benefits of the forum have been so great and I am so grateful for the generous brides that have been so busy planning their own fabulous weddings and still made it a priority to share for the rest of us.  [\/font][\/color]\n[color=rgb(40,40,40)][font=arial]\nWe are getting married June 20, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess.  We have been to this resort twice and love, love, love, love it!!  We are really looking forward to going back and just feeling absolutely confident in the service and quality of the hotel.  So my head has been clouded with to-do lists and I had been really overwhelmed as soon as we transitioned from 2014 to 2015.  I have a destination wedding planner but I found that it was easy to tuck it away and it is over 200 pages so it&#039;s easy to miss a section.  [\/font][\/color]\n[color=rgb(40,40,40)][font=arial]\nWe decided to experiment with a wall map.  We put up some bristol board on a wall at home and my fiance and I started posting all the random things that we need to get done.  All those little things like, \"ask our flower girl\"  or \"write vows\" or \"lose 60lbs\" haha. [\/font][\/color]\n[color=rgb(40,40,40)][font=arial]\nAfter mapping out our to do list it really helped put everything into perspective.  As we get things done, we remove the sticky, and as we think of more things to do, we slap them on.  It has really helped out and I have a better sense of what still needs to get done!  Yay planning!  xo[\/font][\/color]\n[\/quote]Yay another planning thread!!\n\nI totally love the bristol board idea :D, maybe I should do the same. I&#039;m such a visual person and I have this long mental list of things that need to get done, but I&#039;m having a hard time organizing them on paper. The biggest thing right now for us that is that for a couple of months it&#039;s all based on my income. Right now I have a lot of things to buy, but I have to pace it according to the funds. \n\nCan&#039;t wait to read more! :D","Attachments":[],"Id":1886532,"PostDate":1424134412,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>veryvalero, on 16 February 2015 - 11:18 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">Well, I guess it is my turn to start my own planning thread! \u00a0I had read so many helpful planning threads on this awesome forum and I thought I would do the same.<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">I am 124 days away until my wedding (but who is counting) and I thought I would post my ideas to not only help others, but also as a way to keep me accountable to my planning. \u00a0 I have truly loved reading other bride's planning threads and will try to share as much as possible to help someone else in their early stages of planning. \u00a0The benefits of the forum have been so great and I am so grateful for the generous brides that have been so busy planning their own fabulous weddings and still made it a priority to share for the rest of us. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">We are getting married June 20, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess. \u00a0We have been to this resort twice and love, love, love, love it!! \u00a0We are really looking forward to going back and just feeling absolutely confident in the service and quality of the hotel. \u00a0So my head has been clouded with to-do lists and I had been really overwhelmed as soon as we transitioned from 2014 to 2015. \u00a0I have a destination wedding planner but I found that it was easy to tuck it away and it is over 200 pages so it's easy to miss a section. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">We decided to experiment with a wall map. \u00a0We put up some bristol board on a wall at home and my fiance and I started posting all the random things that we need to get done. \u00a0All those little things like, \"ask our flower girl\" \u00a0or \"write vows\" or \"lose 60lbs\" haha.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">After mapping out our to do list it really helped put everything into perspective. \u00a0As we get things done, we remove the sticky, and as we think of more things to do, we slap them on. \u00a0It has really helped out and I have a better sense of what still needs to get done! \u00a0Yay planning! \u00a0xo<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Yay another planning thread!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I totally love the bristol board idea <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/>, maybe I should do the same. I'm such a visual person and I have this long mental list of things that need to get done, but I'm having a hard time organizing them on paper. The biggest thing right now for us that is that for a couple of months it's all based on my income. Right now I have a lot of things to buy, but I have to pace it according to the funds.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Can't wait to read more! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359745104,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.134.151.211","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"96061cafad38c92509e9579efe34683a","RawContent":"Okay so this may be the dumbest question ever but how do you start a planning thread is it under your own account or you just start a post and call it a thread? I&#039;m really enjoying reading everyones posts planning threads and want to start one but not sure how haha. I&#039;m new to this site and just learning how it works.","Attachments":[],"Id":1886541,"PostDate":1424141132,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Okay so this may be the dumbest question ever but how do you start a planning thread is it under your own account or you just start a post and call it a thread? I'm really enjoying reading everyones posts planning threads and want to start one but not sure how haha. I'm new to this site and just learning how it works.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78846-steelethespotlights-planning-thread-may-152015-hard-rock-vallara\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78846-steelethespotlights-planning-thread-may-152015-hard-rock-vallara\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\n\u00a0","Email":"keegan.steele@gmail.com","IpAddress":"50.134.151.211","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1423271759,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282025.jpg?_r=1423455490","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"SteeleTheSpotlight","Id":282025,"Name":"SteeleTheSpotlight","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e361905a3762b1bd97f93a55ca9ccba5","RawContent":"Yay congrats on starting your thread!!!  I should have done a list like yours so fianc\u00e9 would have helped more haha jk! I made one on my iPhone!! Felt great when it was done!!\n\n\n@[member=\"SteeleTheSpotlight\"]\n\nYou just start a post :)\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1886550,"PostDate":1424164042,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Yay congrats on starting your thread!!!  I should have done a list like yours so fianc\u00e9 would have helped more haha jk! I made one on my iPhone!! Felt great when it was done!!<br><br>\n@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"282025\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.phpuser\/282025-steelethespotlight\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">SteeleTheSpotlight<\/span><\/a><br>\nYou just start a post <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399410602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"120c84eb7ddcec017cb16751b0fc5608","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@Calgarybride2015&amp;nbsp; you totally inspired me to make this planning board!&amp;nbsp; You are soooo organized and I was soo impressed with your planning thread.&amp;nbsp; Can&#039;t wait to post more!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Tumblers are up next! xoxo&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886566,"PostDate":1424167703,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@Calgarybride2015\u00a0 you totally inspired me to make this planning board!\u00a0 You are soooo organized and I was soo impressed with your planning thread.\u00a0 Can't wait to post more!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Tumblers are up next! xoxo<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10747;0\/st\/20150620\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/f3ff\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1396964852,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1428501609","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":196,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"76.68.33.151","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a5a14fb00d51708b816f60f5ca555375","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Tumblers!! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So we went back and forth with this idea. &amp;nbsp;We searched and searched different websites and it started adding up really quickly with the customized printing. &amp;nbsp;(We&#039;re canadian) The dollar went up and suddenly it was starting to look like the tumblers could cost us anywhere from $300-$500 for 60 tumblers. &amp;nbsp; We were starting to think we were going to have to scrap the whole idea.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I really wanted tumblers. &amp;nbsp;I attended a DW in Jamaica a few years ago and the tumbler was a gift and we all totally used it. &amp;nbsp;Avoided visiting the bar as often and it was so helpful to use at the beach and pool. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;We found a cool DIY way to have tumblers and all for $2 a piece. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We compared tumblers from Dollar Tree ($1.25) and Dollarama ($2). &amp;nbsp;The dollarama cups appeared to be better quality. &amp;nbsp;They seemed thicker and the straws seemed like they would last at least the entire week! &amp;nbsp;haha. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our logo was designed by KaspiParty from Etsy and we included our wedding hashtag (we finally decided on one and we love it!)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The logo was printed on a clear permanent adhesive and through my fiance we were able to get that for free! &amp;nbsp;yay! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So in total the tumblers cost us $140 ($120 for the cups and $20 for the logo designs)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We are so excited! &amp;nbsp;We still haven&#039;t decided on whether we are doing totes yet. &amp;nbsp;There seems to be a clear divide about whether guests actually use them etc etc. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;One more thing to cross off my list! &amp;nbsp;yay! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;xoxo&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[{"Id":30652,"Name":"IMG_2643.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_02_2015\/post-277519-0-12037500-1424225203.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_02_2015\/post-277519-0-12037500-1424225203_thumb.jpg","Width":1000,"Height":1000},{"Id":30653,"Name":"FullSizeRender (1).jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_02_2015\/post-277519-0-15290200-1424225222.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_02_2015\/post-277519-0-15290200-1424225222_thumb.jpg","Width":640,"Height":740}],"Id":1886659,"PostDate":1424207257,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Tumblers!! \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So we went back and forth with this idea. \u00a0We searched and searched different websites and it started adding up really quickly with the customized printing. \u00a0(We're canadian) The dollar went up and suddenly it was starting to look like the tumblers could cost us anywhere from $300-$500 for 60 tumblers. \u00a0 We were starting to think we were going to have to scrap the whole idea.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I really wanted tumblers. \u00a0I attended a DW in Jamaica a few years ago and the tumbler was a gift and we all totally used it. \u00a0Avoided visiting the bar as often and it was so helpful to use at the beach and pool. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0We found a cool DIY way to have tumblers and all for $2 a piece. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We compared tumblers from Dollar Tree ($1.25) and Dollarama ($2). \u00a0The dollarama cups appeared to be better quality. \u00a0They seemed thicker and the straws seemed like they would last at least the entire week! \u00a0haha. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our logo was designed by KaspiParty from Etsy and we included our wedding hashtag (we finally decided on one and we love it!)\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The logo was printed on a clear permanent adhesive and through my fiance we were able to get that for free! \u00a0yay! \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So in total the tumblers cost us $140 ($120 for the cups and $20 for the logo designs)\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are so excited! \u00a0We still haven't decided on whether we are doing totes yet. \u00a0There seems to be a clear divide about whether guests actually use them etc etc. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>One more thing to cross off my list! \u00a0yay! \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>xoxo<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10747;0\/st\/20150620\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/f3ff\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1396964852,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1428501609","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":196,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.113.233.65","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1e80ba0fdedf166b81ec6088f8c2e60a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Ohh I like your logo!&amp;nbsp; We had an arrow theme too but much simpler.&amp;nbsp; Yours looks awesome and the cups turned out great!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886662,"PostDate":1424208189,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Ohh I like your logo!\u00a0 We had an arrow theme too but much simpler.\u00a0 Yours looks awesome and the cups turned out great!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>Married December 19, 2014 at Beach Palace Resort in Cancun, Mexico<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Wedding Review<\/p>\n<p>Part 1 - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881197'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881197<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Part 2 - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881590'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881590<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Part 3 - <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881861'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/77763-tygrrlilys-planning-thread-beach-palace-resort-121914\/?p=1881861<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"lilyluu83@gmail.com","IpAddress":"174.119.162.30","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1395591348,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277296.jpg?_r=1421643766","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"tygrrlily","Id":277296,"Name":"tygrrlily","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"76.68.33.151","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0d18c98be314fc829a288857ea595cb0","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"tygrrlily\"] &amp;nbsp;Thanks! &amp;nbsp;We loved the arrows so much and we thought it was so appropriate as we got engaged on Valentine&#039;s day! &amp;nbsp;:)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886671,"PostDate":1424213345,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277296\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.phpuser\/277296-tygrrlily\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">tygrrlily<\/span><\/a> \u00a0Thanks! \u00a0We loved the arrows so much and we thought it was so appropriate as we got engaged on Valentine's day! \u00a0<img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10747;0\/st\/20150620\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/f3ff\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>My planning thread:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78801-veryvaleros-wedding-planning-thread-grand-sunset-princess\/<\/a>","Email":"rebecca.valero@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.112.94.76","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1396964852,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277519.jpg?_r=1428501609","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":196,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"veryvalentine","Id":277519,"Name":"veryvalentine","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"acd6bad2614546d7fd821dfad216b8bc","RawContent":"Awesome! Love them! We had the dollar store cups. I recommend packing them all safely including the straws. We had none break but used a lot of bubble wrap!\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1886676,"PostDate":1424213635,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Awesome! Love them! We had the dollar store cups. I recommend packing them all safely including the straws. We had none break but used a lot of bubble wrap!<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399410602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.47.27.141","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78801,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"adfa689d77e2541fe122c2bc76f1fabd","RawContent":"[quote name=\"veryvalero\" post=\"1886526\" timestamp=\"1424146728\"]\nWell, I guess it is my turn to start my own planning thread!  I had read so many helpful planning threads on this awesome forum and I thought I would do the same.\nI am 124 days away until my wedding (but who is counting) and I thought I would post my ideas to not only help others, but also as a way to keep me accountable to my planning.   I have truly loved reading other bride&#039;s planning threads and will try to share as much as possible to help someone else in their early stages of planning.  The benefits of the forum have been so great and I am so grateful for the generous brides that have been so busy planning their own fabulous weddings and still made it a priority to share for the rest of us.  \n \nWe are getting married June 20, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess.  We have been to this resort twice and love, love, love, love it!!  We are really looking forward to going back and just feeling absolutely confident in the service and quality of the hotel.  So my head has been clouded with to-do lists and I had been really overwhelmed as soon as we transitioned from 2014 to 2015.  I have a destination wedding planner but I found that it was easy to tuck it away and it is over 200 pages so it&#039;s easy to miss a section.  \n \nWe decided to experiment with a wall map.  We put up some bristol board on a wall at home and my fiance and I started posting all the random things that we need to get done.  All those little things like, \"ask our flower girl\"  or \"write vows\" or \"lose 60lbs\" haha. \n \nAfter mapping out our to do list it really helped put everything into perspective.  As we get things done, we remove the sticky, and as we think of more things to do, we slap them on.  It has really helped out and I have a better sense of what still needs to get done!  Yay planning!  xo[\/quote]I created a bristol board last night! I have a clearer picture of what needs to be done. On the other hand, I also realized I was missing a few key components.\n\nThanks for the idea!","Attachments":[],"Id":1886688,"PostDate":1424240424,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>veryvalero, on 16 February 2015 - 11:18 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>Well, I guess it is my turn to start my own planning thread! \u00a0I had read so many helpful planning threads on this awesome forum and I thought I would do the same.<br>\nI am 124 days away until my wedding (but who is counting) and I thought I would post my ideas to not only help others, but also as a way to keep me accountable to my planning. \u00a0 I have truly loved reading other bride's planning threads and will try to share as much as possible to help someone else in their early stages of planning. \u00a0The benefits of the forum have been so great and I am so grateful for the generous brides that have been so busy planning their own fabulous weddings and still made it a priority to share for the rest of us. \u00a0<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nWe are getting married June 20, 2015 at the Grand Sunset Princess. \u00a0We have been to this resort twice and love, love, love, love it!! \u00a0We are really looking forward to going back and just feeling absolutely confident in the service and quality of the hotel. \u00a0So my head has been clouded with to-do lists and I had been really overwhelmed as soon as we transitioned from 2014 to 2015. \u00a0I have a destination wedding planner but I found that it was easy to tuck it away and it is over 200 pages so it's easy to miss a section. \u00a0<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nWe decided to experiment with a wall map. \u00a0We put up some bristol board on a wall at home and my fiance and I started posting all the random things that we need to get done. \u00a0All those little things like, \"ask our flower girl\" \u00a0or \"write vows\" or \"lose 60lbs\" haha.\u00a0<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nAfter mapping out our to do list it really helped put everything into perspective. \u00a0As we get things done, we remove the sticky, and as we think of more things to do, we slap them on. \u00a0It has really helped out and I have a better sense of what still needs to get done! \u00a0Yay planning! \u00a0xo<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nI created a bristol board last night! I have a clearer picture of what needs to be done. On the other hand, I also realized I was missing a few key components.<br><br>\nThanks for the idea! \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"carter.watson2015@gmail.com","IpAddress":"71.47.13.201","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1393520930,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-276925.jpg?_r=1393540000","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AyeWatSoon","Id":276925,"Name":"AyeWatSoon","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":289,"TotalPages":29,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":280},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":1,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
